Comparison with reference values computed independently
(photon mass lambda^2 = 1e-30 GeV^2, deltauv = 0, mu = 100 GeV,
alpha(0) = 0.72973525694968e-2, me = 0.510998950e-3, mmu = 105.658375e-3,
m_pi from the reference momenta, mtau = model default).

  cd examples/eepp_sqed/check_ref  && make run            # e+e- -> pi+pi-
  cd examples/eeppA_sqed/check_ref && python3 check_vp.py # e+e- -> pi+pi- A

Both use the already compiled virtual/ libraries; parameters are set in
check_ref.f90 before initgolem() (which runs ew_ren with them).

What is compared:
  - photon-mass result = GoSam finite part at mu^2 = lambda^2
    (1/eps_IR -> ln(lambda^2/mu^2); no double pole, on-shell UV
    renormalisation does not depend on mu), nlo_prefactors = 2;
  - the reference SUMS over the e-, e+ spins: GoSam x 4;
  - the reference has NO vacuum polarisation in the virtual photon:
    2 Re[Pi_ren(q^2) ...] of the e, mu, tau, phi loops is subtracted
    analytically (2->2: in check_ref.f90; 2->3: check_vp.py, with the ISR
    (q^2 = s') and FSR (q^2 = s) tree amplitudes computed from scratch and
    checked against the GoSam Born);
  - GoSam leg order e-, e+, phi+, phi-, A: reference p4 (pi+) and p3 (pi-)
    are swapped.

Result (2026-11-12):
  2->2  Born 1.7e-15,  virtual - VP  4.8e-9
  2->3  Born 1.3e-14,  virtual - VP  1.7e-8
  (without the VP subtraction the virtual differs by 0.87% and 0.86%).
SOFT is not computed by GoSam and is not compared.

Variant without vacuum polarisation in GoSam
--------------------------------------------
eepp_novp.rc / eeppA_novp.rc (process_path=virtual_novp) add the card
option
  vacpol=false
(model sqed_ct only), which
  - drops the one-loop diagrams without a photon in the loop, i.e. the
    closed loops of leptons and phi (bubbles on the photon line, the phi
    seagull snail, the 3-photon triangles of 2->3 that sum to zero by
    Furry/C), on top of any filter.nlo;
  - sets the Fortran parameter vacpol = .false. in common/ew_ct.f90
    (ew_ct_sqed.f90), so dZ_AA = dZ_e = 0. dZ_AA enters only the photon
    two-point counterterm gctA, because dZ_e + dZ_AA/2 = 0 in the vertices.
The counterterm diagrams are not filtered (they use filter.lo).

  cd examples/eepp_sqed  && ../../build/bin/gosam.py eepp_novp.rc \
       && make -C virtual_novp source compile        # python 2.7 in PATH
  cd examples/eeppA_sqed && ../../build/bin/gosam.py eeppA_novp.rc \
       && make -C virtual_novp source compile
  cd examples/eepp_sqed/check_ref  && make run NOVP=1
  cd examples/eeppA_sqed/check_ref && make run NOVP=1   # or python3 check_vp.py

Result (2026-11-12): same numbers as the analytic subtraction,
  2->2 virtual 4.8e-9, 2->3 virtual 1.7e-8 relative to the reference,
  poles unchanged (UV still cancels), and the VP of GoSam
  (full - no-VP) equals the formula to 4e-14 in 2->3 (ISR + FSR, with
  the imaginary parts).
